WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:09.457
[♪ epic theme music playing]

2
00:01:56.606 --> 00:01:58.608
[wind lightly whooshing]

3
00:02:05.448 --> 00:02:08.451
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

4
00:02:17.126 --> 00:02:19.128
[horse nickering]

5
00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.092
[horse nickering]

6
00:02:26.427 --> 00:02:28.429
[heavy doors open]

7
00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:43.694
[Rhaenyra] [echoing voice]
<i>Helaena.</i>

8
00:02:45.655 --> 00:02:47.031
<i>Helaena.</i>

9
00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:49.784
[voice clear]
<i>Helaena.</i>

10
00:02:50.952 --> 00:02:52.328
[gasps lightly]

11
00:02:58.042 --> 00:03:00.253
I'm sorry to disturb
your rest.

12
00:03:00.294 --> 00:03:02.755
Have you heard w-word
from my mother?

13
00:03:02.797 --> 00:03:04.173
No.

14
00:03:04.215 --> 00:03:06.217
Nor do I expect to. until...

15
00:03:09.178 --> 00:03:11.180
[birdsong]

16
00:03:18.646 --> 00:03:21.816
Did Aemond ask you
to ride into battle with him?

17
00:03:25.403 --> 00:03:26.779
Hm.

18
00:03:26.821 --> 00:03:28.406
Lord Corlys
imagined he would.

19
00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:34.161
When I was a girl.
I wanted to fly.

20
00:03:35.746 --> 00:03:37.331
But now. when...

21
00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:40.167
when I'm with Dreamfyre...

22
00:03:44.505 --> 00:03:45.590
it's...

23
00:03:47.341 --> 00:03:49.093
and then too much.

24
00:03:53.681 --> 00:03:57.226
I think our father
felt the same way.

25
00:03:57.268 --> 00:03:59.061
He renounced
the strength of dragons

26
00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:00.730
and embraced a quieter life.

27
00:04:00.771 --> 00:04:02.607
He did not wish
to be changed.

28
00:04:03.858 --> 00:04:08.112
You believe the dragons
alter us in some way?

29
00:04:10.406 --> 00:04:12.074
You now have many dragons.

30
00:04:13.034 --> 00:04:15.453
Are you yourself not altered?

31
00:04:16.412 --> 00:04:17.872
[scoffs] No.

32
00:04:18.956 --> 00:04:21.751
Well. I do not wish to be.

33
00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:27.048
I wished only
to put an end to our contest

34
00:04:27.089 --> 00:04:29.342
and restore us
to our proper order.

35
00:04:29.383 --> 00:04:30.801
[sighs]

36
00:04:32.261 --> 00:04:33.429
Helaena.

37
00:04:35.056 --> 00:04:38.559
Sister. I believe that you...

38
00:04:39.769 --> 00:04:42.396
may be a dreamer.

39
00:04:43.564 --> 00:04:44.732
That you...

40
00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.401
see things.

41
00:04:50.279 --> 00:04:52.990
I see f-flashes sometimes.

42
00:04:54.116 --> 00:04:55.993
Some cl-clearer
than others.

43
00:04:57.828 --> 00:04:59.413
What did you see last?

44
00:05:02.291 --> 00:05:03.626
A gray mare.

45
00:05:06.587 --> 00:05:07.588
Mm-hmm.

46
00:05:10.091 --> 00:05:12.259
What of Daemon?
Have you seen him?

47
00:05:14.762 --> 00:05:15.763
Hm?

48
00:05:17.306 --> 00:05:18.808
The Winter Wolves. then.

49
00:05:19.809 --> 00:05:21.519
Or Tumbleton.

50
00:05:23.104 --> 00:05:25.606
Will Ormund Hightower
be brought to heel?

51
00:05:25.648 --> 00:05:27.233
I don't know.

52
00:05:27.274 --> 00:05:29.944
You don't know?
Or you will not say?

53
00:05:36.492 --> 00:05:38.911
You may refuse me
as your sister.

54
00:05:38.953 --> 00:05:40.579
but I may compel you
as your queen.

55
00:05:40.621 --> 00:05:42.999
Now. tell me what you know!

56
00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:46.168
Tell me there has been
no mistake.

57
00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.129
that I will prevail.

58
00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.297
as the gods must surely intend.
Tell me.

59
00:06:03.561 --> 00:06:06.564
♪

60
00:06:22.371 --> 00:06:23.664
[grunting]

61
00:06:26.709 --> 00:06:27.877
[groaning]

62
00:06:33.716 --> 00:06:34.842
Mother.

63
00:06:36.218 --> 00:06:39.180
I told you I would come.
if I could.

64
00:06:41.432 --> 00:06:44.351
Were you not taken captive?

65
00:06:46.604 --> 00:06:48.022
Your sister was taken.

66
00:06:49.774 --> 00:06:51.776
But I managed
to stay hidden. to escape.

67
00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:56.864
You have been so clever
to remain here undiscovered.

68
00:06:58.365 --> 00:06:59.950
I thought all had
forsaken me.

69
00:07:02.203 --> 00:07:03.537
[sighs]

70
00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:13.255
How could I forsake...

71
00:07:14.048 --> 00:07:15.299
my best...

72
00:07:16.759 --> 00:07:18.219
and truest son?

73
00:07:20.721 --> 00:07:22.640
The city has fallen. Aemond.

74
00:07:24.725 --> 00:07:26.727
- [soft kiss]
- You're all I have left.

75
00:07:34.944 --> 00:07:36.779
[Alicent sighs]

76
00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.118
The road has been long
and perilous.

77
00:07:42.159 --> 00:07:43.577
so I'll be glad of a bed.

78
00:07:45.955 --> 00:07:47.790
What of Aegon?

79
00:07:49.583 --> 00:07:52.503
Aegon is most likely dead.

80
00:07:55.673 --> 00:07:57.258
I did all I could.

81
00:08:04.265 --> 00:08:05.599
And for you.

82
00:08:12.648 --> 00:08:14.483
[whispering]
But I have failed you. Aemond.

83
00:08:14.525 --> 00:08:15.526
No.

84
00:08:17.361 --> 00:08:19.405
- I was too young.
- Never.

85
00:08:19.446 --> 00:08:21.031
I was just a child.

86
00:08:23.117 --> 00:08:25.202
[sighs. sniffles]

87
00:08:57.902 --> 00:08:59.904
[Alicent moaning]

88
00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.957
And in this moment
I will give you a son.

89
00:09:11.999 --> 00:09:14.376
[Aemond moaning]

90
00:09:14.418 --> 00:09:15.878
Aemond.

91
00:09:22.176 --> 00:09:23.552
Aemond.

92
00:09:24.762 --> 00:09:26.764
- What have you seen?
- [gasps] Please.

93
00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.862
[creatures chittering]

94
00:09:43.697 --> 00:09:45.366
[footsteps approaching]

95
00:09:49.954 --> 00:09:51.455
Aemond.

96
00:09:54.917 --> 00:09:57.920
[♪ dramatic music playing]

97
00:10:23.487 --> 00:10:25.072
[Gwayne] Open the gates!

98
00:10:27.074 --> 00:10:29.076
[people chattering]

99
00:10:34.623 --> 00:10:36.625
[chattering continues]

100
00:10:45.426 --> 00:10:47.261
They've crossed
the Blackwater Rush.

101
00:10:47.303 --> 00:10:49.430
- How many?
- Twenty thousand.

102
00:10:49.471 --> 00:10:51.181
A day's march away.
Two at most.

103
00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:56.228
So. your dim
but ambitious Dornish friend

104
00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.771
died in the mud for nothing.

105
00:10:58.772 --> 00:10:59.898
That is no matter.

106
00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:01.567
I have a piece
on the board now

107
00:11:01.608 --> 00:11:03.277
that will bring the bitch
to her knees.

108
00:11:06.113 --> 00:11:07.614
And what is that?

109
00:11:14.705 --> 00:11:16.040
[sighs]

110
00:11:20.627 --> 00:11:22.629
[Caraxes bellowing]

111
00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.842
[whistling]

112
00:11:39.521 --> 00:11:41.523
[chittering]

113
00:11:44.693 --> 00:11:46.153
- My prince...
- Move!

114
00:11:49.656 --> 00:11:51.825
Where is she?
Where's Rhaena?

115
00:11:52.743 --> 00:11:54.995
I see we are dispensing
with courtesies.

116
00:11:55.037 --> 00:11:56.663
Is she here?

117
00:11:57.664 --> 00:12:01.710
She flew. just after
I sent to you.

118
00:12:01.752 --> 00:12:03.337
I could not hold her.

119
00:12:03.379 --> 00:12:06.090
Put her in chains
if you have to. lock her in a cell.

120
00:12:07.341 --> 00:12:09.134
Do you imagine it's so easy
to force a dragonrider

121
00:12:09.176 --> 00:12:10.886
to do what she does not wish?

122
00:12:12.221 --> 00:12:13.472
She exposes me. too.

123
00:12:13.514 --> 00:12:15.474
She beseeched me
with tears in her eyes.

124
00:12:15.516 --> 00:12:17.518
swore that she would
remain here in hiding.

125
00:12:19.186 --> 00:12:22.147
Talk of a dragonrider
is rife in the Vale.

126
00:12:22.189 --> 00:12:24.733
The villagers gossip
of a wild girl in the mountains

127
00:12:24.775 --> 00:12:26.318
living amongst
nettles and sheep.

128
00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.404
I am finished
with the matter.

129
00:12:28.445 --> 00:12:30.197
It is in my best interest now
to alert the queen

130
00:12:30.239 --> 00:12:31.865
- to her flight.
- No.

131
00:12:32.783 --> 00:12:34.326
You may blunt
Rhaenyra's wrath.

132
00:12:34.368 --> 00:12:36.203
but you will not evade it.
Give me a day.

133
00:12:43.877 --> 00:12:45.295
Please.

134
00:12:48.757 --> 00:12:51.969
She has been here and there
seeking news of Vhagar.

135
00:12:53.637 --> 00:12:55.681
There's word of a sighting
near Fairmarket.

136
00:12:55.722 --> 00:12:57.433
so I can only assume...

137
00:13:01.812 --> 00:13:04.523
[dragon vocalizing]

138
00:13:04.565 --> 00:13:06.567
[Baela] We are two days
behind Aemond at best.

139
00:13:07.568 --> 00:13:10.446
I have long tired
of this endless searching.

140
00:13:11.947 --> 00:13:15.033
I cannot help but think
I'm being punished by Rhaenyra.

141
00:13:15.075 --> 00:13:17.119
or at least sent far
from her sight.

142
00:13:18.912 --> 00:13:21.248
She thinks of us
only as tools to be wielded.

143
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:26.795
I wondered. my lady.
if I might beg you for a kindness.

144
00:13:26.837 --> 00:13:30.048
My father wishes for Alyn
and me to be legitimized

145
00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.426
and take the Velaryon name.

146
00:13:32.468 --> 00:13:35.554
The queen
is being reluctant.

147
00:13:35.596 --> 00:13:37.431
You know my standing
after the Gullet.

148
00:13:38.307 --> 00:13:40.517
I do not think my words
would have much sway with her.

149
00:13:42.436 --> 00:13:44.146
But your father. perhaps.

150
00:13:45.314 --> 00:13:48.150
Why this concern now
with names and titles?

151
00:13:48.192 --> 00:13:50.444
- [dragon screeching]
- I understand your grievance.

152
00:13:50.486 --> 00:13:52.654
but surely. you have
a better thing in your dragon

153
00:13:52.696 --> 00:13:54.907
than any lordly appellation.

154
00:13:54.948 --> 00:13:57.159
It is only that
if either of us were to marry.

155
00:13:57.201 --> 00:13:59.411
That is...

156
00:13:59.453 --> 00:14:03.457
if either of us gained the favor
of some highborn lady.

157
00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:05.959
[scoffs]

158
00:14:06.001 --> 00:14:09.129
He has spoken to you. then.
Your brother.

159
00:14:13.133 --> 00:14:15.802
[dragons bellowing]

160
00:14:17.679 --> 00:14:19.389
Is it Vhagar?

161
00:14:22.976 --> 00:14:23.977
No.

162
00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.022
I did not think us like
to escape the Red Keep.

163
00:14:27.064 --> 00:14:29.816
But Ser Adrian remained
steadfast and resolute.

164
00:14:31.151 --> 00:14:33.445
He led us
to a secret gate. and...

165
00:14:33.487 --> 00:14:36.114
and I had enough coin
with me for horses.

166
00:14:36.156 --> 00:14:37.950
We tried to remain
off the roads.

167
00:14:37.991 --> 00:14:41.995
but the forests have become
impassable in places.

168
00:14:42.037 --> 00:14:43.664
There are wild men
in the woods now.

169
00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.875
I would not have arrived here
if it wasn't for him.

170
00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:49.794
Rhaenyra took the castle.
but he remained loyal.

171
00:14:49.795 --> 00:14:51.838
He helped me at great risk
to his own person.

172
00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.590
He is a gr... [gasps]

173
00:14:57.052 --> 00:14:58.428
Have I offended you?

174
00:15:03.267 --> 00:15:04.518
No.

175
00:15:11.024 --> 00:15:12.693
You are all I have left.

176
00:15:16.947 --> 00:15:19.283
- [footsteps receding]
- [sighs]

177
00:15:21.201 --> 00:15:23.203
[footsteps approaching]

178
00:15:28.542 --> 00:15:30.377
This is he.

179
00:15:30.419 --> 00:15:32.546
my protector and guide.
Ser Adrian.

180
00:15:32.588 --> 00:15:33.922
Your Grace.

181
00:15:37.968 --> 00:15:38.969
Mm.

182
00:15:45.267 --> 00:15:46.435
[sighs]

183
00:15:49.563 --> 00:15:52.566
Well. it seems
I owe you a debt.

184
00:15:55.319 --> 00:15:57.779
I did only
as my conscience demanded.

185
00:15:59.948 --> 00:16:02.242
The queen dowager
was treated shamefully.

186
00:16:13.587 --> 00:16:15.255
- [blade thwacking]
- [Alicent] Aemond!

187
00:16:15.297 --> 00:16:16.673
[gurgling]

188
00:16:18.133 --> 00:16:19.468
[body thuds]

189
00:16:24.598 --> 00:16:26.266
Sorry. Mother.

190
00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:31.647
There are secrets here.
and I can trust no stranger.

191
00:16:32.689 --> 00:16:34.608
[Alys] Ah. there you are.

192
00:16:36.443 --> 00:16:38.111
You're just in time
for supper.

193
00:16:42.282 --> 00:16:44.493
[liquid pouring]

194
00:16:44.534 --> 00:16:47.079
The maesters tell me
the fat of livestock

195
00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:48.789
is beneficial to the bones.

196
00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:51.750
But I do wonder how something
so slippery in substance

197
00:16:51.792 --> 00:16:54.670
can truly be benign.
[chuckles]

198
00:16:55.796 --> 00:16:58.298
Do try the wine. Lord Corlys.

199
00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:01.468
I find it wards off
the fetid air of this place.

200
00:17:03.679 --> 00:17:04.680
Mm.

201
00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.309
What are you about.
Hightower?

202
00:17:09.351 --> 00:17:11.978
Is this some kind
of final repast?

203
00:17:12.896 --> 00:17:15.440
Pigeon pie before
the executioner's block?

204
00:17:15.482 --> 00:17:16.817
On the contrary.

205
00:17:17.859 --> 00:17:19.695
We hope to enjoy
the pleasure of your company

206
00:17:19.736 --> 00:17:21.279
for quite some time.

207
00:17:21.321 --> 00:17:24.366
You will be of great assistance
to us in our little endeavor.

208
00:17:25.575 --> 00:17:28.870
- As what? A hostage?
- Hm.

209
00:17:30.038 --> 00:17:32.124
Does the savage queen
harbor such a tender heart

210
00:17:32.165 --> 00:17:34.167
that she should
cast away her crown

211
00:17:34.209 --> 00:17:35.794
for the sake of her
wayward Hand?

212
00:17:35.836 --> 00:17:37.170
I think not.

213
00:17:38.714 --> 00:17:40.799
The Velaryons. however.

214
00:17:40.841 --> 00:17:43.677
with their lord as forfeit.
the men of Driftmark

215
00:17:43.719 --> 00:17:46.804
will think better
of entering King's Landing.

216
00:17:46.805 --> 00:17:50.434
And without them. the city will again
eat of its own disorder.

217
00:17:54.271 --> 00:17:56.314
H-How will that help

218
00:17:56.356 --> 00:17:58.525
when the Winter Wolves
are clawing at our gates?

219
00:18:05.866 --> 00:18:07.242
Do you know?

220
00:18:07.284 --> 00:18:10.412
More and more I am inclined

221
00:18:10.454 --> 00:18:11.913
to limit my diet...

222
00:18:13.457 --> 00:18:14.875
to the vegetable kingdom.

223
00:18:16.251 --> 00:18:18.170
Just as the people of Naathi do.

224
00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:21.214
If you have finished
with your instruction...

225
00:18:21.256 --> 00:18:23.049
What do you see in them. anyway?

226
00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:25.552
The Targaryen...

227
00:18:27.053 --> 00:18:28.180
element.

228
00:18:28.221 --> 00:18:29.931
You are a traveled man.

229
00:18:29.973 --> 00:18:32.267
you have seen
the world's wonders.

230
00:18:33.435 --> 00:18:35.729
Why limit yourself
in tedious alliance

231
00:18:35.771 --> 00:18:37.981
to the brutish
and the incurious?

232
00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:44.196
Your wife. of course.
was of their blood.

233
00:18:44.237 --> 00:18:46.448
That ended all too predictably.

234
00:18:49.284 --> 00:18:51.870
I would think.
after having seen

235
00:18:51.912 --> 00:18:53.955
how they devour
one of their own...

236
00:18:57.083 --> 00:18:58.794
I would like to return
to my cell.

237
00:19:00.003 --> 00:19:01.463
As you please.

238
00:19:05.759 --> 00:19:07.052
Oh. Lord Corlys?

239
00:19:07.093 --> 00:19:08.303
Before you go...

240
00:19:10.013 --> 00:19:11.932
He was in uncommon
good spirits...

241
00:19:13.058 --> 00:19:15.393
as though he were on the eve
of some great victory.

242
00:19:15.435 --> 00:19:17.729
He seems to believe that
with Lord Corlys as hos...

243
00:19:17.771 --> 00:19:19.523
Is this his
"piece on the board"?

244
00:19:21.274 --> 00:19:23.318
What does the order or disorder
of King's Landing

245
00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.570
matter to us now
with an army at the gates?

246
00:19:25.612 --> 00:19:27.531
I'm supposed to be the king.

247
00:19:29.783 --> 00:19:31.660
What sort of ruler am I?

248
00:19:31.701 --> 00:19:34.412
Am I to sit by impotent
while a madman

249
00:19:34.454 --> 00:19:36.122
offers us up
for the slaughter?

250
00:19:38.041 --> 00:19:39.960
And all of our men with us?

251
00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.338
Seems there's no escaping it.

252
00:19:44.422 --> 00:19:47.717
The dream some have of covering themselves
in everlasting glory...

253
00:19:49.219 --> 00:19:51.555
of somehow transcending
humanity's common fate.

254
00:19:55.016 --> 00:19:58.812
I am sorry about your friend.

255
00:20:00.313 --> 00:20:02.107
[sniffling]

256
00:20:02.148 --> 00:20:04.234
He gave himself to the dust.

257
00:20:10.323 --> 00:20:12.117
I could order the army
to surrender.

258
00:20:12.158 --> 00:20:14.202
[scoffs]
And then what?

259
00:20:14.244 --> 00:20:16.162
Have us all marched
to the gallows?

260
00:20:18.832 --> 00:20:21.751
You could fly away
on Tessarion.

261
00:20:23.003 --> 00:20:24.337
Without you
as a pretext for...

262
00:20:24.379 --> 00:20:26.339
He would continue
as he began.

263
00:20:28.091 --> 00:20:30.134
Where would I go?

264
00:20:30.135 --> 00:20:33.346
Who would receive a king who
left his own men to their ruin?

265
00:20:36.558 --> 00:20:38.894
I have no fear
of insignificance. Gwayne.

266
00:20:42.898 --> 00:20:45.108
Rhaenyra may keep her crown.
for all I care.

267
00:20:47.402 --> 00:20:49.153
[chuckles softly]

268
00:20:49.154 --> 00:20:50.822
[Torrhen Manderly]
Frankly. it is outrageous.

269
00:20:50.864 --> 00:20:54.034
There is a campaign against me!
Jeering in the streets.

270
00:20:54.075 --> 00:20:57.329
My own daughter found
the doorstep of my city dwelling

271
00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:00.290
smeared with some sort of
foul matter.

272
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.169
I don't know what you
want me to do about it.

273
00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:05.420
My queen.

274
00:21:06.254 --> 00:21:07.422
With respect.

275
00:21:08.757 --> 00:21:11.885
In front of petitioners.
you named me responsible

276
00:21:11.927 --> 00:21:15.263
for the current financial
grievances in the city.

277
00:21:15.305 --> 00:21:16.598
I hardly be...

278
00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:18.058
Well. what have you done
to alleviate them?

279
00:21:19.059 --> 00:21:21.853
What can I do?

280
00:21:21.895 --> 00:21:24.731
I have advocated for a tax.
It has fallen on deaf ears.

281
00:21:25.523 --> 00:21:29.611
Our dribbles of gold are spent
as fast as they are gathered.

282
00:21:29.653 --> 00:21:32.029
It's as if I have been
installed here

283
00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:34.074
as some sort of scapegoat.

284
00:21:38.411 --> 00:21:40.246
Has there been any word
from Lord Corlys?

285
00:21:42.123 --> 00:21:43.416
From Harrenhal?

286
00:21:46.586 --> 00:21:49.756
- And Daemon?
- [Orwyle] Absent.

287
00:21:49.798 --> 00:21:54.052
The prince is on some...
errand of his own.

288
00:21:54.094 --> 00:21:57.722
The Keepers say he flew out
of the city before dawn.

289
00:21:57.764 --> 00:21:59.724
The river host
are but a day's march

290
00:21:59.766 --> 00:22:01.393
from Tumbleton. Your Grace.

291
00:22:01.434 --> 00:22:03.979
and the Velaryon forces will be
at King's Landing on the morrow.

292
00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.315
I have a reputation
to uphold.

293
00:22:07.357 --> 00:22:10.276
If Ser Adrian
has been successful

294
00:22:10.318 --> 00:22:12.904
in his endeavor. of course.

295
00:22:12.946 --> 00:22:15.573
then there is the small matter
of Harrenhal...

296
00:22:15.615 --> 00:22:17.867
Just take it.

297
00:22:18.827 --> 00:22:20.412
Your Grace?

298
00:22:20.453 --> 00:22:22.580
Return to the Twins

299
00:22:22.622 --> 00:22:25.959
and lead the men you have
left there to Harrenhal.

300
00:22:26.001 --> 00:22:27.794
[gasps]

301
00:22:27.836 --> 00:22:30.088
This I will do gladly!

302
00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:32.089
If Aemond is dead.
all the better.

303
00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:34.175
But in any case. you shall occupy it again.
and leave no place

304
00:22:34.217 --> 00:22:35.343
- for him to return.
- [door opens]

305
00:22:35.385 --> 00:22:37.220
- [Addam] My queen.
- [footsteps approaching]

306
00:22:39.139 --> 00:22:41.099
We have seen
something strange.

307
00:22:41.141 --> 00:22:42.684
- Vhagar?
- No.

308
00:22:42.726 --> 00:22:44.769
Sheepstealer.
In the Riverlands.

309
00:22:44.811 --> 00:22:46.730
on the banks of the Blue Fork
near Fairmarket.

310
00:22:47.731 --> 00:22:49.357
That is unexpected.
He's not known...

311
00:22:49.399 --> 00:22:51.192
Your Grace. he has a rider.

312
00:22:52.485 --> 00:22:55.196
- A new rider?
- I could not say.

313
00:22:55.238 --> 00:22:57.449
We gave chase.
but lost him in the hills.

314
00:22:57.490 --> 00:22:59.492
[high-pitch ringing.
sounds muffling]

315
00:23:02.704 --> 00:23:04.706
That head
Daemon brought to you.

316
00:23:04.748 --> 00:23:06.875
can you say in honesty
you've had no doubts?

317
00:23:06.916 --> 00:23:09.878
He was long in the Riverlands.
and now Sheepstealer

318
00:23:09.919 --> 00:23:12.881
is sighted there with a rider
he assured you was dead.

319
00:23:12.922 --> 00:23:14.841
And in that same moment.

320
00:23:14.883 --> 00:23:17.510
he has absented himself
without explanation.

321
00:23:17.552 --> 00:23:19.803
I have known him to lie.
but this is a great...

322
00:23:19.804 --> 00:23:22.891
You and I have known him to be
capable of far worse than lies.

323
00:23:22.932 --> 00:23:25.185
He has chafed
since you arrived here

324
00:23:25.226 --> 00:23:27.187
over your restraint
in wielding power.

325
00:23:27.228 --> 00:23:29.480
He is impetuous
and impatient.

326
00:23:29.481 --> 00:23:31.858
Who can say what alliance
he may have formed in secret

327
00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:35.070
- when he found you lacking.
- He has sworn to serve me.

328
00:23:36.404 --> 00:23:38.740
I cannot believe that now.
when I need him most.

329
00:23:38.782 --> 00:23:40.241
- that he would...
- Forgive me.

330
00:23:45.371 --> 00:23:46.539
Your Grace.

331
00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:52.212
But is there anything
Daemon could do

332
00:23:52.253 --> 00:23:54.464
that you would truly
not believe?

333
00:23:59.385 --> 00:24:01.054
Fetch Ser Addam.

334
00:24:09.437 --> 00:24:11.606
They say it is the strength
of the sun in Volantis

335
00:24:11.648 --> 00:24:13.566
that makes for such sweetness
in the grape.

336
00:24:15.068 --> 00:24:17.278
If you mean to console me
for this folly

337
00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:19.781
with Volantene wines.
you're much mistaken.

338
00:24:19.823 --> 00:24:22.450
Your Grace.
I beg you. reconsider.

339
00:24:22.492 --> 00:24:25.453
At Maidenpool. we might take ship
for Casterly Rock instead.

340
00:24:25.495 --> 00:24:27.914
[Aegon]
No. I am decided on Braavos.

341
00:24:27.956 --> 00:24:30.041
How much further
must we ride?

342
00:24:30.083 --> 00:24:31.584
Some days still to the port.

343
00:24:32.585 --> 00:24:34.629
Braavos will prove itself
a most cultivated city.

344
00:24:34.671 --> 00:24:36.589
- I assure you.
- [pig squealing]

345
00:24:36.631 --> 00:24:38.133
Perhaps even
a home from home.

346
00:24:38.174 --> 00:24:39.634
[pig squealing]

347
00:24:42.846 --> 00:24:43.930
Whoa.

348
00:24:44.681 --> 00:24:47.433
My good woman.
what is it you flee?

349
00:24:47.475 --> 00:24:49.102
An army marches this way.

350
00:24:49.144 --> 00:24:51.396
- Some thousand strong.
- Which army?

351
00:24:51.437 --> 00:24:53.982
My daughter said she saw
the red fish on the white.

352
00:24:54.023 --> 00:24:56.568
- The Mootons.
- That's where we are going. to Maidenpool.

353
00:24:56.609 --> 00:24:59.237
We must keep moving.
Turn back if you can.

354
00:24:59.279 --> 00:25:00.780
Mootons are sworn to Rhaenyra.

355
00:25:02.282 --> 00:25:03.867
They can't have
heard about me?

356
00:25:06.161 --> 00:25:07.162
Hyah.

357
00:25:07.203 --> 00:25:10.206
[♪ dramatic music playing]

358
00:25:13.001 --> 00:25:15.003
[distant people chattering]

359
00:25:17.130 --> 00:25:18.631
[Tyland]
The road is lost to us.

360
00:25:19.632 --> 00:25:22.093
We must fall back
to Rook's Rest.

361
00:25:22.135 --> 00:25:24.596
We can't go back there.
We may have been discovered.

362
00:25:24.637 --> 00:25:27.473
There is an army coming for us
and we have no place to shelter.

363
00:25:28.892 --> 00:25:30.185
There are thick walls
at Rook's Rest

364
00:25:30.226 --> 00:25:31.811
and enough men
to defend them.

365
00:25:31.853 --> 00:25:34.981
It shall be refuge for His Grace
till Mooton's host has passed.

366
00:25:36.983 --> 00:25:39.819
[utensils clacking]

367
00:25:39.861 --> 00:25:41.821
- [Aemond] Mm.
- [Alys] You must be famished.

368
00:25:43.239 --> 00:25:45.200
It's a long journey
from King's Landing.

369
00:25:47.660 --> 00:25:48.661
Yes.

370
00:25:50.663 --> 00:25:52.040
And fraught. no doubt.

371
00:25:53.499 --> 00:25:55.585
If half the tales I have heard
about the King's Road are true.

372
00:25:59.172 --> 00:26:01.466
How is it that the two of you

373
00:26:01.507 --> 00:26:04.385
- came to know one another?
- Mm.

374
00:26:07.096 --> 00:26:08.514
She saved my life.

375
00:26:10.683 --> 00:26:12.310
At whose behest?

376
00:26:12.352 --> 00:26:14.145
Your lord's?

377
00:26:14.187 --> 00:26:16.022
I generally follow
my own dictates.

378
00:26:18.691 --> 00:26:21.361
[laughing] Aemond. I still don't
understand who this woman is.

379
00:26:21.402 --> 00:26:23.238
[sighs]

380
00:26:23.279 --> 00:26:24.405
Mm.

381
00:26:25.698 --> 00:26:27.700
She is a lady.

382
00:26:29.244 --> 00:26:31.037
And a maester. of sorts.

383
00:26:33.248 --> 00:26:36.084
The care of the castle
has fallen to her for now.

384
00:26:38.544 --> 00:26:41.881
I've decided
to stay here with her

385
00:26:41.923 --> 00:26:43.549
and make this place my seat.

386
00:26:46.135 --> 00:26:47.887
Your seat?

387
00:26:47.929 --> 00:26:49.931
Was that not what you
yourself suggested?

388
00:26:51.224 --> 00:26:52.934
A new fortress
from which to rule.

389
00:26:52.976 --> 00:26:56.853
Rhaenyra has the throne
and six dragons to her name.

390
00:26:56.854 --> 00:27:00.024
It is she who rules now. as much as we
might wish it otherwise.

391
00:27:00.066 --> 00:27:01.234
Mm.

392
00:27:01.276 --> 00:27:04.988
Rhaenyra's dragons
are ridden by commoners.

393
00:27:06.656 --> 00:27:10.535
She's defiled our great house.
diminished the Iron Throne.

394
00:27:10.576 --> 00:27:12.578
and sowed the seeds
of her own ruin.

395
00:27:14.247 --> 00:27:15.748
She will certainly fail.

396
00:27:18.293 --> 00:27:20.962
And we will raise
our own throne.

397
00:27:22.672 --> 00:27:25.758
In the mud of the Riverlands.

398
00:27:27.844 --> 00:27:29.345
A new dawn is coming.

399
00:27:32.265 --> 00:27:34.475
A new line of unsullied kings.

400
00:27:37.812 --> 00:27:39.522
We need only to bide our time.

401
00:27:41.941 --> 00:27:43.443
And you. Mother.

402
00:27:45.320 --> 00:27:47.113
You will wait with us.

403
00:27:48.614 --> 00:27:50.783
You have worth yet to offer.

404
00:27:50.825 --> 00:27:53.619
I'm sure your mother
will wish to move on.

405
00:27:55.038 --> 00:27:57.457
Back to Oldtown. perhaps.

406
00:27:57.498 --> 00:27:59.584
Our climate
doesn't seem to suit her.

407
00:27:59.625 --> 00:28:02.337
Mm. there's nothing for her there.
I am all she has left.

408
00:28:02.378 --> 00:28:03.838
- [Alicent] There is Helaena.
- No!

409
00:28:04.672 --> 00:28:06.174
You'll stay with us.

410
00:28:11.054 --> 00:28:12.555
We're out of wood.

411
00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:16.351
[plate clattering]

412
00:28:20.355 --> 00:28:23.775
I will not be coddled or admonished
like a witless child.

413
00:28:23.816 --> 00:28:25.985
Tread carefully
with her. Aemond.

414
00:28:27.070 --> 00:28:28.946
She's come to do you some ill.

415
00:28:28.988 --> 00:28:30.698
She is my blood.

416
00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:33.284
- [wood chopping]
- And thus without blemish?

417
00:28:33.326 --> 00:28:36.287
She's always had her secrets.
most of them poorly kept.

418
00:28:37.330 --> 00:28:41.042
My designs for our future
did not include your mother.

419
00:28:41.084 --> 00:28:42.502
And there is the truth of it.

420
00:28:43.461 --> 00:28:45.004
You want me for yourself.

421
00:28:47.090 --> 00:28:49.050
There is a fog
that surrounds her.

422
00:28:51.594 --> 00:28:54.055
She has come
to do you some evil.

423
00:28:55.681 --> 00:28:58.351
You would be wise to keep
your dark thoughts to yourself.

424
00:29:06.401 --> 00:29:09.404
You Targaryen boys all want
the same thing. don't you?

425
00:29:14.534 --> 00:29:16.536
[panting]

426
00:29:19.247 --> 00:29:20.540
[sniffling]

427
00:29:22.208 --> 00:29:24.210
[breathing heavily]

428
00:29:26.212 --> 00:29:29.215
[♪ dramatic music playing]

429
00:29:55.825 --> 00:29:57.952
- [panicked chatter]
- [baby crying]

430
00:30:01.414 --> 00:30:02.748
Tom Tangletongue. what news?

431
00:30:03.624 --> 00:30:06.878
Lord Mooton of Maidenpool.
he's dispatched an army.

432
00:30:06.919 --> 00:30:08.588
They're marching in haste.

433
00:30:10.006 --> 00:30:13.259
Have you not seen our Janos?
I thought he'd be with you.

434
00:30:14.260 --> 00:30:15.886
No. Where are they marching?

435
00:30:15.887 --> 00:30:18.055
They were commanded here.
to Rook's Rest.

436
00:30:18.097 --> 00:30:20.892
But they're going
village to village. it seems.

437
00:30:20.933 --> 00:30:23.019
in search
of your friend Lannister.

438
00:30:24.145 --> 00:30:26.355
Something about
the queen's gold.

439
00:30:27.064 --> 00:30:29.859
They'll be here before w-we know it.
You'd best be on the move.

440
00:30:33.029 --> 00:30:34.280
[groaning]

441
00:30:35.364 --> 00:30:36.616
[grunting]

442
00:30:41.996 --> 00:30:43.414
I think you'll agree.
Ser Tyland.

443
00:30:43.456 --> 00:30:44.790
that you should
give yourself up.

444
00:30:45.625 --> 00:30:47.001
She will flay me alive.

445
00:30:47.043 --> 00:30:49.587
No doubt.
But once Mooton has you in hand.

446
00:30:49.629 --> 00:30:51.589
he'll turn towards King's Landing.
and His Grace and I

447
00:30:51.631 --> 00:30:54.175
- may yet slip away.
- Give the king to me and my men.

448
00:30:54.217 --> 00:30:56.177
We will ride hard
and escape Mooton's clutches.

449
00:30:56.219 --> 00:30:58.179
Oh. must you be so thick?

450
00:30:58.221 --> 00:30:59.847
Rhaenyra is hunting you.

451
00:30:59.889 --> 00:31:01.974
His Grace is not safe
in your company.

452
00:31:02.016 --> 00:31:04.268
Turn yourself in
and give him the chance to flee.

453
00:31:04.310 --> 00:31:05.478
[Tyland] Him or you?

454
00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:07.480
[Larys]
It is the honorable thing to do.

455
00:31:07.522 --> 00:31:09.482
- Your Grace. for now. at least...
- No.

456
00:31:12.151 --> 00:31:13.528
No.

457
00:31:13.569 --> 00:31:15.196
Go where you will.

458
00:31:16.155 --> 00:31:17.365
Both of you.

459
00:31:18.407 --> 00:31:20.034
Preserve your own skins.

460
00:31:21.327 --> 00:31:22.870
But I shall run no more.

461
00:31:22.912 --> 00:31:24.956
If you do not run.
Your Grace. you will die.

462
00:31:24.997 --> 00:31:26.290
Then I'll die.

463
00:31:26.332 --> 00:31:28.000
But not as a fugitive.

464
00:31:30.336 --> 00:31:33.130
Unknown.
Covered in dust.

465
00:31:33.172 --> 00:31:37.843
Not with an arrow in my back
or trapped like a fox in a hole.

466
00:31:39.095 --> 00:31:41.138
This... this is absurd.
Ser Tyland. I entreat you

467
00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:43.391
- to reason with His Grace.
- I'll make my stand here.

468
00:31:44.767 --> 00:31:46.936
Mm.
And be buried as a king.

469
00:31:48.604 --> 00:31:50.022
With my dragon.

470
00:31:53.818 --> 00:31:56.320
I will not have the histories
say that I was slain

471
00:31:56.362 --> 00:31:58.698
in ignominy
by my own brother.

472
00:32:05.037 --> 00:32:07.123
If the king wishes
to remain. then...

473
00:32:09.375 --> 00:32:11.168
I shall remain with him.

474
00:32:11.210 --> 00:32:13.296
I cannot leave him to face
an army meant for me.

475
00:32:16.382 --> 00:32:18.092
[horses neighing]

476
00:32:21.637 --> 00:32:23.389
You're resolved in this then?

477
00:32:30.730 --> 00:32:32.064
Well then. my lords...

478
00:32:33.566 --> 00:32:36.152
it seems there is only one thing
left for me to do.

479
00:32:37.653 --> 00:32:39.572
May the Seven
be ever at your side.

480
00:32:39.614 --> 00:32:41.574
[Tyland]
You would abandon your master?

481
00:32:41.616 --> 00:32:43.951
I am a cripple. Ser Tyland.

482
00:32:46.078 --> 00:32:48.205
Humble enough to admit
that my presence in a fight

483
00:32:48.247 --> 00:32:49.790
would make
no earthly difference.

484
00:32:52.835 --> 00:32:55.254
Of course. if my king
commanded me to stay...

485
00:32:57.256 --> 00:32:58.966
What Lord Larys says is true.

486
00:33:01.010 --> 00:33:02.970
He would be no use to us here.

487
00:33:04.096 --> 00:33:05.264
Well. then.

488
00:33:07.016 --> 00:33:10.186
It will be my duty to see
that King Aegon is remembered.

489
00:33:12.146 --> 00:33:15.483
His heroic last hours
immortalized through story...

490
00:33:15.524 --> 00:33:17.151
- [chuckles softly]
- ...and song.

491
00:33:21.280 --> 00:33:22.615
Your Grace.

492
00:33:32.124 --> 00:33:33.793
[sighs]

493
00:33:36.629 --> 00:33:37.963
Your Grace.

494
00:33:39.048 --> 00:33:40.341
Come. come. come.

495
00:33:53.229 --> 00:33:55.231
[Sheepstealer bellowing]

496
00:33:59.318 --> 00:34:00.736
[screeching]

497
00:34:02.321 --> 00:34:04.573
[Caraxes whistling]

498
00:34:05.741 --> 00:34:07.743
[chittering]

499
00:34:10.162 --> 00:34:11.872
[bellowing]

500
00:34:19.505 --> 00:34:22.508
[dragons screeching.
bellowing]

501
00:34:31.016 --> 00:34:32.893
- Stay back!
- You swore to me.

502
00:34:32.935 --> 00:34:35.020
- You should not have come.
- Did you think she would not hear of this?

503
00:34:35.062 --> 00:34:37.940
Stay back!
He does not heed me!

504
00:34:39.108 --> 00:34:41.193
[roaring]

505
00:34:42.570 --> 00:34:43.696
Daor!

506
00:34:45.239 --> 00:34:47.241
[screeching]

507
00:34:49.076 --> 00:34:50.119
Daor!

508
00:34:57.042 --> 00:34:59.211
What do you hope to do here?
In the reeds and the mud?

509
00:34:59.253 --> 00:35:00.921
Vhagar was here.

510
00:35:00.963 --> 00:35:02.381
Or near here. last I heard.

511
00:35:02.423 --> 00:35:03.924
We heard the same.
but she is gone.

512
00:35:03.966 --> 00:35:05.426
Then I will fly
in search of her.

513
00:35:05.468 --> 00:35:07.511
And if you find her?

514
00:35:07.553 --> 00:35:09.764
I thought I could do this.
but I can't.

515
00:35:09.805 --> 00:35:12.892
I cannot live the way I have.
cut off from all who loved me.

516
00:35:13.559 --> 00:35:15.936
And so. you think by going
after Vhagar. you will...

517
00:35:17.229 --> 00:35:18.355
what?

518
00:35:18.397 --> 00:35:20.065
If I kill her.

519
00:35:20.107 --> 00:35:22.026
I will have paid
some of my debt to Rhaenyra.

520
00:35:22.067 --> 00:35:24.236
I would at least have grounds
to sue for her mercy.

521
00:35:24.278 --> 00:35:26.363
- You will more likely die.
- Then I will have paid all of it.

522
00:35:26.405 --> 00:35:28.783
I will die absolved
if I cannot live that way.

523
00:35:29.742 --> 00:35:31.744
[Sheepstealer roars]

524
00:35:38.751 --> 00:35:40.002
Let me help you. then.

525
00:35:41.587 --> 00:35:43.255
You cannot battle Vhagar alone.

526
00:35:44.465 --> 00:35:46.258
But the two of us
may yet prevail.

527
00:35:48.010 --> 00:35:49.595
Why would you do
such a thing?

528
00:35:51.263 --> 00:35:52.765
I had no dragon either
when I was young.

529
00:35:52.807 --> 00:35:53.933
Did you know that?

530
00:35:55.309 --> 00:35:57.978
My mother died in childbed
when I was three years of age.

531
00:35:58.020 --> 00:35:59.897
My brother sank into sadness.

532
00:35:59.939 --> 00:36:02.274
I was alone.
just as you have been.

533
00:36:06.111 --> 00:36:07.780
I should have done better.
Rhaena.

534
00:36:10.115 --> 00:36:12.117
[Caraxes whistling]

535
00:36:16.163 --> 00:36:19.083
- You lie.
- I did not summon them.

536
00:36:19.124 --> 00:36:22.419
- You'd betray your own daughter?
- I have not. I swear it.

537
00:36:22.461 --> 00:36:23.754
She does not yet know
who you are.

538
00:36:23.796 --> 00:36:25.673
[bellowing]

539
00:36:25.714 --> 00:36:26.841
[Daemon] Leave him.

540
00:36:26.882 --> 00:36:28.551
They will tear you
from the sky.

541
00:36:30.135 --> 00:36:31.262
[whimpering]

542
00:36:31.303 --> 00:36:33.013
Run! Run!

543
00:36:37.142 --> 00:36:38.811
[dragon roaring]

544
00:36:43.357 --> 00:36:45.734
[dragons bellowing]

545
00:36:47.570 --> 00:36:48.863
Go!

546
00:36:56.370 --> 00:36:58.372
[dragons vocalizing]

547
00:37:00.040 --> 00:37:02.042
[speaking High Valyrian]

548
00:37:03.669 --> 00:37:05.212
- Call off your dragon!
- What is your agreement

549
00:37:05.254 --> 00:37:08.340
with Sheepstealer's rider?
Answer carefully.

550
00:37:08.382 --> 00:37:10.342
You will not have
another chance to deceive me.

551
00:37:10.384 --> 00:37:11.844
I never wished to deceive you.

552
00:37:11.886 --> 00:37:13.679
- Then. speak!
- Call off your dragon.

553
00:37:13.721 --> 00:37:16.891
[dragons bellowing]

554
00:37:18.851 --> 00:37:20.644
[grunting]

555
00:37:20.686 --> 00:37:21.979
[Rhaena shouting]

556
00:37:22.021 --> 00:37:24.231
Please. Rhaenyra.

557
00:37:24.273 --> 00:37:25.691
She's not herself.

558
00:37:26.692 --> 00:37:28.694
- [Rhaena shouting]
- [dragons vocalizing]

559
00:37:39.914 --> 00:37:41.040
Rhaena?

560
00:37:46.128 --> 00:37:47.588
It wasn't you.

561
00:37:57.890 --> 00:38:00.517
She was Sheepstealer's rider?

562
00:38:00.559 --> 00:38:02.561
All this time. you knew.

563
00:38:07.232 --> 00:38:08.734
This is finished!

564
00:38:15.574 --> 00:38:18.285
[dragons roaring]

565
00:38:21.121 --> 00:38:22.122
Move!

566
00:38:23.415 --> 00:38:25.417
[roaring continues]

567
00:38:59.284 --> 00:39:00.661
[shouting in High Valyrian]

568
00:39:00.703 --> 00:39:02.705
[screeching]

569
00:39:12.548 --> 00:39:15.801
- Your Grace!
- Help Daemon! Go!

570
00:39:16.969 --> 00:39:18.012
Go!

571
00:39:18.053 --> 00:39:20.055
[dragons continue roaring]

572
00:39:24.143 --> 00:39:25.894
[Rhaenyra shouting]

573
00:39:31.150 --> 00:39:32.776
[gasping]

574
00:39:32.818 --> 00:39:33.986
With me!

575
00:39:39.867 --> 00:39:41.452
[screeching]

576
00:39:41.493 --> 00:39:42.911
No!

577
00:39:46.540 --> 00:39:48.542
[screeching continues]

578
00:39:51.587 --> 00:39:54.548
Escort the queen.
I will finish this.

579
00:40:09.563 --> 00:40:11.273
[screeching]

580
00:40:22.534 --> 00:40:24.203
[grunting]

581
00:40:24.244 --> 00:40:26.246
[Yelping. screeching]

582
00:40:31.085 --> 00:40:33.087
[grunting]

583
00:40:45.432 --> 00:40:47.059
[whimpers]

584
00:40:54.441 --> 00:40:57.194
[Mysaria]
It is magnificent in its way.

585
00:40:57.236 --> 00:41:00.656
[Madam Sylvi] I saw it once before when
I petitioned the queen.

586
00:41:04.910 --> 00:41:07.246
Do you know
what it brings to my mind?

587
00:41:08.288 --> 00:41:11.834
A hundred sharp little cocks
all vying for attention.

588
00:41:13.460 --> 00:41:15.546
The queen wishes
at the moment

589
00:41:15.587 --> 00:41:17.923
to hear no more petitions.

590
00:41:18.924 --> 00:41:20.425
That is a mistake.

591
00:41:21.343 --> 00:41:22.886
I agree.

592
00:41:22.928 --> 00:41:25.180
There is villainy and violence
on her streets now.

593
00:41:27.099 --> 00:41:29.059
The people are afraid
to go out by night.

594
00:41:29.101 --> 00:41:30.936
It is to her detriment only.

595
00:41:31.854 --> 00:41:33.564
Those who look
to her for relief

596
00:41:33.605 --> 00:41:36.024
now feel she's turned
her back on them.

597
00:41:38.944 --> 00:41:42.739
I wished to hear from you
how you fare in this city.

598
00:41:42.781 --> 00:41:45.576
And if there are others
who may find it a consolation

599
00:41:45.617 --> 00:41:47.661
to come to me
with their troubles

600
00:41:47.703 --> 00:41:49.454
and have them considered.

601
00:41:50.789 --> 00:41:53.750
You make yourself her proxy.

602
00:41:53.792 --> 00:41:55.752
Someone must.
Do you not agree?

603
00:41:55.794 --> 00:41:57.921
If she herself is reluctant.

604
00:41:57.963 --> 00:42:01.090
I can perhaps then bring
certain dilemmas before her

605
00:42:01.091 --> 00:42:04.678
when I judge her mood
to be more accommodating.

606
00:42:07.472 --> 00:42:09.474
You are changed.

607
00:42:12.311 --> 00:42:16.356
This... has changed you.

608
00:42:16.398 --> 00:42:20.152
My heart is with the downtrodden
as it has ever been.

609
00:42:20.194 --> 00:42:21.862
Is it?

610
00:42:21.904 --> 00:42:23.947
Or have you styled yourself
a champion

611
00:42:23.989 --> 00:42:25.699
in order to access these halls?

612
00:42:28.076 --> 00:42:29.161
Look at you.

613
00:42:30.162 --> 00:42:31.622
Standing at the foot
of the throne

614
00:42:31.663 --> 00:42:33.957
wearing a silk worth a year
of my earnings.

615
00:42:33.999 --> 00:42:36.335
promising to whisper
into the ear of a queen.

616
00:42:37.669 --> 00:42:40.631
You thrill now to a tune
you once abhorred.

617
00:42:40.672 --> 00:42:43.383
Does it not occur to you
that from this position

618
00:42:43.425 --> 00:42:45.886
I may help those
who have no avenue?

619
00:42:45.928 --> 00:42:49.181
What power
do you have in truth?

620
00:42:50.599 --> 00:42:52.684
Except to flatter and cajole?

621
00:42:55.938 --> 00:42:56.939
Ah.

622
00:42:57.940 --> 00:42:59.483
Is that why
you called me here?

623
00:43:00.567 --> 00:43:03.528
To look on the trappings so that
someone would hold you in awe?

624
00:43:06.198 --> 00:43:07.783
This was a mistake.

625
00:43:09.243 --> 00:43:11.495
How common
I must seem to you.

626
00:43:11.536 --> 00:43:12.871
That will be all.

627
00:43:15.916 --> 00:43:18.085
Some advice. my lady.

628
00:43:19.419 --> 00:43:22.005
These people
are not your own.

629
00:43:22.047 --> 00:43:23.882
You would do well
to remember that.

630
00:43:25.217 --> 00:43:27.261
Within the walls
of the highborn.

631
00:43:27.302 --> 00:43:31.390
a whore will always and ever
remain a whore.

632
00:43:36.228 --> 00:43:38.230
[footsteps receding]

633
00:43:39.231 --> 00:43:41.233
[dragons bellowing]

634
00:43:41.275 --> 00:43:44.278
[♪ dramatic music playing]

635
00:43:47.281 --> 00:43:49.283
[bellowing continues]

636
00:43:53.912 --> 00:43:55.580
Find her a room.

637
00:43:55.622 --> 00:43:57.249
I do not wish to see her.

638
00:44:03.755 --> 00:44:05.090
[Alicent] Aemond?

639
00:44:08.427 --> 00:44:09.594
Mother.

640
00:44:21.189 --> 00:44:22.733
Your friend Alys.

641
00:44:22.774 --> 00:44:24.484
- She's not my friend.
- Oh.

642
00:44:25.861 --> 00:44:28.155
She doesn't want me
to stay here.

643
00:44:28.196 --> 00:44:30.907
If I'm disturbing
some understanding between...

644
00:44:30.949 --> 00:44:32.242
No.

645
00:44:32.284 --> 00:44:34.328
- I should perhaps not have come.
- No.

646
00:44:34.369 --> 00:44:36.955
I will... I will take my leave.
if that would behoove you.

647
00:44:38.540 --> 00:44:40.167
I'm glad you came.

648
00:44:44.129 --> 00:44:45.630
I brought you something.

649
00:44:47.382 --> 00:44:48.633
[cup scraping]

650
00:44:51.470 --> 00:44:52.971
Spiced wine.

651
00:44:54.890 --> 00:44:57.809
I remember a time when you would
not fall asleep without it.

652
00:45:04.399 --> 00:45:06.026
Alys doesn't trust you.

653
00:45:14.993 --> 00:45:16.495
Who do you trust?

654
00:45:20.874 --> 00:45:21.875
I...

655
00:45:23.543 --> 00:45:25.420
I tried to kill Aegon.

656
00:45:35.514 --> 00:45:36.598
I know.

657
00:45:39.518 --> 00:45:40.936
[whispering]
My dear...

658
00:45:42.687 --> 00:45:44.106
foolish boy.

659
00:45:55.867 --> 00:45:57.285
Your Grace.

660
00:45:59.371 --> 00:46:01.039
[door opens]

661
00:46:05.210 --> 00:46:06.878
- [door closes]
- No. stay.

662
00:46:22.561 --> 00:46:24.396
She implored me
not to tell you.

663
00:46:31.319 --> 00:46:33.864
She could not face you.
I wished only to protect her.

664
00:46:33.905 --> 00:46:35.031
From what?

665
00:46:35.073 --> 00:46:36.575
What do you think I am?

666
00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:40.537
Y-You are my wife.

667
00:46:40.579 --> 00:46:44.124
She's my daughter.
One I-I-I have long neglected.

668
00:46:47.294 --> 00:46:50.922
Was she not seeking. in all this.
my favor or yours?

669
00:46:53.133 --> 00:46:57.804
I have looked a hundred times
at that skull you brought...

670
00:46:59.514 --> 00:47:02.350
thinking it was the villain
who killed my son.

671
00:47:06.313 --> 00:47:08.064
I am sorry.

672
00:47:08.106 --> 00:47:11.026
but you must see now that
I kept no scheme against you.

673
00:47:13.361 --> 00:47:15.697
I did only what I thought
was best. Rhaenyra.

674
00:47:20.535 --> 00:47:21.703
Please.

675
00:47:25.624 --> 00:47:26.958
It's late.

676
00:47:43.225 --> 00:47:46.770
[door opens. closes]

677
00:47:46.811 --> 00:47:49.814
[♪ somber music playing]

678
00:48:03.078 --> 00:48:04.496
[whispering] I am sorry.

679
00:48:06.748 --> 00:48:08.041
To Jace.

680
00:48:10.877 --> 00:48:12.629
To you.
You would have been queen.

681
00:48:12.671 --> 00:48:13.964
[Baela] Enough.

682
00:48:14.005 --> 00:48:17.008
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

683
00:48:33.858 --> 00:48:35.360
You will begin anew.

684
00:48:43.201 --> 00:48:46.371
[Alyn] More Hightower loyalists were found.
Alert the confessors.

685
00:48:50.792 --> 00:48:52.210
[guard] Ser Alyn.

686
00:48:53.461 --> 00:48:54.754
It was left for you.

687
00:49:09.436 --> 00:49:11.855
[breathing shakily]

688
00:49:11.896 --> 00:49:13.231
[owl screeching]

689
00:49:14.441 --> 00:49:16.443
[bird squawking]

690
00:49:26.494 --> 00:49:28.246
[thud]

691
00:49:28.288 --> 00:49:29.289
Alys.

692
00:49:33.835 --> 00:49:35.086
Idiot.

693
00:49:37.922 --> 00:49:40.925
[♪ dramatic music playing]

694
00:50:06.785 --> 00:50:09.120
[screaming]

695
00:50:11.623 --> 00:50:13.625
[baby crying]

696
00:50:19.547 --> 00:50:21.549
[baby continues crying]

697
00:50:26.054 --> 00:50:27.138
[whimpers]

698
00:50:31.142 --> 00:50:32.310
[gasps]

699
00:50:35.563 --> 00:50:37.565
[Dreamfyre chirping]

700
00:50:41.069 --> 00:50:42.821
[snarling and screeching]

701
00:50:45.657 --> 00:50:47.492
Dracarys!

702
00:50:53.206 --> 00:50:55.291
[chickens clucking]

703
00:50:55.333 --> 00:50:58.336
[♪ gentle music playing]

704
00:51:05.844 --> 00:51:07.846
[wind whistling]

705
00:51:14.894 --> 00:51:16.896
[distorted noises intensifying]

706
00:51:22.193 --> 00:51:24.195
[fire crackling softly]

707
00:51:29.451 --> 00:51:32.454
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

708
00:51:47.135 --> 00:51:48.887
[bones rattling]

709
00:51:53.099 --> 00:51:56.060
[Rhaenyra] It was Rhaena
he was hiding all along.

710
00:51:58.938 --> 00:52:01.357
He lied.
I did not lead you astray.

711
00:52:01.399 --> 00:52:04.110
And yet you cannot say
he betrayed me

712
00:52:04.152 --> 00:52:06.529
so much as he would not
betray his daughter.

713
00:52:06.571 --> 00:52:07.947
This time.

714
00:52:07.989 --> 00:52:10.867
But does it not prove
he is willing to deceive you

715
00:52:10.909 --> 00:52:12.786
- if he judges it necessary?
- [scoffs]

716
00:52:13.620 --> 00:52:15.622
And you've never done the same?

717
00:52:15.663 --> 00:52:17.707
I've acted only
in your interests.

718
00:52:17.749 --> 00:52:19.918
You have sought
to turn me from him.

719
00:52:21.002 --> 00:52:24.923
Pouring your honey in my ear.
whispering. encouraging.

720
00:52:24.964 --> 00:52:27.258
seeking to make me
in your image.

721
00:52:27.300 --> 00:52:28.968
In my image?

722
00:52:29.010 --> 00:52:32.222
Your Grace. have I ever
counseled you to do aught

723
00:52:32.263 --> 00:52:35.433
but what Viserys
would have you do in his place?

724
00:52:35.475 --> 00:52:38.102
As you have ofttimes said.
is your own desire.

725
00:52:38.144 --> 00:52:41.481
Yes. and in hewing to his vision.
what have I reaped?

726
00:52:42.440 --> 00:52:44.567
Peace?
Prosperity?

727
00:52:44.609 --> 00:52:46.945
Ah. the gratitude
of my subjects.

728
00:52:55.036 --> 00:52:56.788
My father was not a dreamer.

729
00:52:58.289 --> 00:53:00.124
But his whole life
was a dream.

730
00:53:03.711 --> 00:53:05.296
Do not lose faith.

731
00:53:07.131 --> 00:53:10.134
You are on the precipice
of a great victory.

732
00:53:12.136 --> 00:53:14.264
The uncertainties
that oppress you

733
00:53:14.305 --> 00:53:15.807
will soon be resolved.

734
00:53:16.808 --> 00:53:20.311
Those who oppose you
will fall away.

735
00:53:21.729 --> 00:53:25.024
Even Aemond
is all but vanquished.

736
00:53:25.066 --> 00:53:28.403
You will be queen
for many years after this.

737
00:53:29.404 --> 00:53:31.823
And your children's children
after you.

738
00:53:36.995 --> 00:53:38.830
Just a little longer.

739
00:53:44.168 --> 00:53:45.378
Do you think...

740
00:53:46.838 --> 00:53:48.006
I am worthy?

741
00:53:50.675 --> 00:53:52.719
In this moment. my queen.

742
00:53:56.180 --> 00:53:57.765
Rhaenyra.

743
00:54:06.024 --> 00:54:08.359
I have never been
more certain of it.

744
00:54:13.698 --> 00:54:16.701
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

745
00:55:03.331 --> 00:55:06.334
[faint rhythmic beating]

746
00:55:16.094 --> 00:55:18.096
[faint beating continues]

747
00:55:27.438 --> 00:55:29.440
[beating grows louder]

748
00:55:31.609 --> 00:55:34.320
A final stand then.
Ser Tyland.

749
00:55:36.072 --> 00:55:37.532
Your Grace.

750
00:56:06.019 --> 00:56:10.565
We claim this land for Rhaenyra.
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

751
00:56:11.816 --> 00:56:14.027
You will throw down your arms

752
00:56:14.068 --> 00:56:16.362
and make ready
to swear your fealty.

753
00:56:21.492 --> 00:56:23.870
[softly]
Oh. no. no. no. no. no.

754
00:56:23.911 --> 00:56:24.996
[Tyland] Your Grace?

755
00:56:26.914 --> 00:56:28.332
Will you flee after all?

756
00:56:45.975 --> 00:56:48.728
We shall not surrender
to the false queen.

757
00:56:48.770 --> 00:56:50.772
[laughter]

758
00:56:57.028 --> 00:56:59.197
Is that you.
Tyland Lannister?

759
00:57:00.114 --> 00:57:02.033
Your queen's been
looking for you.

760
00:57:03.868 --> 00:57:06.079
Tell us where the gold is.

761
00:57:06.120 --> 00:57:09.207
and you will die
with your ears still attached.

762
00:57:22.804 --> 00:57:24.472
Behold me now!

763
00:57:25.389 --> 00:57:26.891
[horse whinnying]

764
00:57:26.933 --> 00:57:28.893
I am Aegon Targaryen!

765
00:57:30.561 --> 00:57:33.064
- Viserys' true heir!
- [distant bellowing]

766
00:57:33.106 --> 00:57:36.776
The sixth King of the Andals
and the Rhoynar

767
00:57:36.818 --> 00:57:38.361
and the First Men!

768
00:57:38.402 --> 00:57:41.280
I was anointed
by the High Septon

769
00:57:41.322 --> 00:57:43.241
in the light of the Seven.

770
00:57:43.282 --> 00:57:47.495
And it is in their light
that I stand before you now!

771
00:57:49.413 --> 00:57:51.707
Strike me down!

772
00:57:51.749 --> 00:57:54.919
And the Stranger
will take retribution.

773
00:57:56.462 --> 00:58:00.049
The Warrior's sword
will be judgment upon you.

774
00:58:00.091 --> 00:58:02.301
[dragon snarling]

775
00:58:02.343 --> 00:58:04.595
[chuckles] Yes.

776
00:58:04.637 --> 00:58:06.764
Yes. cowards.

777
00:58:07.640 --> 00:58:09.559
- You might well retreat.
- [rumbling]

778
00:58:09.600 --> 00:58:12.478
For now you see me
as I truly am!

779
00:58:12.520 --> 00:58:13.938
- [dragon snarling]
- [gasping softly]

780
00:58:13.980 --> 00:58:16.274
Dreadful in vengeance!

781
00:58:16.315 --> 00:58:19.527
- Righteous and glorious!
- [horses whinnying]

782
00:58:22.655 --> 00:58:24.657
[dragon bellowing
and growling]

783
00:58:26.701 --> 00:58:28.703
[dragon chirping]

784
00:58:30.621 --> 00:58:31.998
[whispering] Sunfyre.

785
00:58:34.292 --> 00:58:36.294
[Sunfyre chittering]

786
00:58:39.297 --> 00:58:40.631
Sunfyre.

787
00:58:42.300 --> 00:58:43.885
Dracarys.

788
00:58:45.803 --> 00:58:48.222
Run! Save yourselves!

789
00:58:49.307 --> 00:58:51.309
[soldiers screaming]

790
00:58:54.020 --> 00:58:56.022
[Aegon yelling]

791
00:58:57.356 --> 00:58:59.358
[screaming continues]

792
00:59:02.153 --> 00:59:04.155
[Aegon continues yelling]

793
00:59:09.160 --> 00:59:11.204
[Aegon laughing]

794
00:59:17.043 --> 00:59:19.170
[bellowing]

795
00:59:28.346 --> 00:59:29.513
Oh.

796
00:59:32.058 --> 00:59:33.392
Decent ale. that.

797
00:59:35.895 --> 00:59:37.438
I thought you might enjoy it.

798
00:59:42.193 --> 00:59:44.904
- [gulping] Mm.
- I have had word...

799
00:59:46.072 --> 00:59:50.076
since we last spoke
of a most distressing incident.

800
00:59:50.117 --> 00:59:53.371
My whisperers tell me that
Daemon Targaryen struck you.

801
00:59:54.538 --> 00:59:55.915
In the street.

802
00:59:58.125 --> 01:00:01.128
In front of all the commoners
passing by.

803
01:00:02.296 --> 01:00:06.384
An intolerable insult
to someone of your stature.

804
01:00:08.386 --> 01:00:12.682
But then. uh. it's almost to be
expected from those people.

805
01:00:12.723 --> 01:00:14.558
She did tell me
not to go into town.

806
01:00:15.393 --> 01:00:17.186
- To be fair.
- Ludicrous.

807
01:00:17.228 --> 01:00:19.397
A man needs his sustenance
and cheer.

808
01:00:21.524 --> 01:00:24.443
But it is obvious
Rhaenyra and her ilk

809
01:00:24.485 --> 01:00:25.945
regard you only as a tool.

810
01:00:27.905 --> 01:00:30.283
To be used and reprimanded.

811
01:00:32.743 --> 01:00:34.578
Whereas I understand...

812
01:00:36.080 --> 01:00:37.456
who you really are.

813
01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:45.256
You said last time...

814
01:00:47.341 --> 01:00:49.302
that you could give me
a lordship.

815
01:00:51.429 --> 01:00:52.763
And a castle.

816
01:00:54.765 --> 01:00:55.850
Honeyholt.

817
01:00:57.685 --> 01:00:58.853
Honeyholt?

818
01:01:00.146 --> 01:01:02.606
[chuckles]
Honeyholt is a trifle.

819
01:01:04.317 --> 01:01:06.944
It seems that
Driftmark itself

820
01:01:06.986 --> 01:01:08.779
may soon be without a master.

821
01:01:10.614 --> 01:01:12.783
Lord of the Tides.

822
01:01:14.785 --> 01:01:16.454
What do you think of that?

823
01:01:22.960 --> 01:01:24.754
- [chuckles]
- [mugs clanking]

824
01:01:24.795 --> 01:01:26.630
They will laugh
at you no more...

825
01:01:27.715 --> 01:01:29.467
when they see you as you are.

826
01:01:33.721 --> 01:01:34.889
No.

827
01:01:36.974 --> 01:01:38.309
They will burn.

828
01:01:49.195 --> 01:01:51.989
♪
